chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Email, texts and push notifications for an advanced course: chapter 20 of the 3rd edition and today's services"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the textbook ontology built over the published chapter. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-01T12:00:00; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.4." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does chapter 20 of the 3rd edition teach about sending and reading email through the Gmail API, about texts through SMS email gateways and about push notifications through ntfy, which of its printed outputs and claims still hold, which parts can be run without an account or a network under Python 3.14.4, and what must an advanced course add so that it matches current services and current Python?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-01." .
